    ret = asn1_decode_simple_ber(etype, der, der_size, &str, &str_size, NULL);
else
    ret = asn1_decode_simple_der(etype, der, der_size, (const uint8_t**)&str, &str_size);
```

For `allow_ber = 1`, `asn1_decode_simple_ber` allocates memory for `str` and fills it with the decoded data. If it succeeds, `str` points to initialized data.

But wait, there's a subtle issue. In `_gnutls_x509_decode_string`:

```c
if (allow_ber)
    free(str);
```

After `memcpy`, if `allow_ber` is true, it frees `str`. But `str` was allocated by `asn1_decode_simple_ber`. If `allow_ber` is false, `str` points to data inside the DER buffer (from `asn1_decode_simple_der`), so it shouldn't be freed.

This looks correct.

